  "description": "The Roslyn analyzer-authoring rules (RS1xxx, RS2xxx) as strongly referenced constants, so that SuppressMessageAttribute takes compile-checked references instead of magic strings. Ids, categories, titles and help links are read from Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.Analyzers' own DiagnosticDescriptor instances — including the two categories that break its own naming pattern. For anyone writing a Roslyn analyzer or code fix. Unofficial; not affiliated with or endorsed by Microsoft.",
